  "artifact": {
    "title": "Project Orion \u2014 The Reilly Protocol Suite: Web4 Reference Implementation",
    "author": "Lawrence Reilly",
    "description": "Live reference implementation of the Web4 architecture, unifying all eighteen active IETF Internet-Drafts of the Reilly Protocol Suite in a single autonomous application. Renders the suite as a continuously verified constellation, with agents operating on both backend and frontend, a human-oversight/autonomous mode toggle, and Triple Verification of every draft against the IETF archive, the FUNET mirror (nic.funet.fi), and the OTEnet mirror (ftp.otenet.gr). All artifacts are anchored under Dual-Layer Digital Permanence: Bitcoin timestamping via OpenTimestamps, Zenodo DOI archival, IPFS, and IETF submission. Deployed at project-orion-production.up.railway.app. Author: Lawrence John Reilly Jr.\r\n\r\nIf the record field has a tight character limit, here's a compact version:\r\n\r\nShort description:\r\nWeb4 reference implementation unifying all 18 IETF Internet-Drafts of the Reilly Protocol Suite \u2014 autonomous agents, human-oversight toggle, Triple Verification (IETF/FUNET/OTEnet), Dual-Layer Digital Permanence. Live at project-orion-production.up.railway.app.",
